<title>UK: GEC's Bates retires, off to Premier Farnell.</title>
<headline>GEC's Bates retires, off to Premier Farnell.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's General Electric Co Plc said on Thursday that its deputy managing director Malcolm Bates is to retire and become non-executive chairman of Premier Farnell Plc.</p>
<p>Bates will retire at the end of the financial year. He takes over from Richard Hanwell, who retired in December, at the electronics components and equipment supplier and distributor.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
